From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:38:07 +0100
Subject: test: run the tests with ctest, and add more

CTest now runs the tests (ctest --test-dir build); they need no display
and take a few seconds.  BUILD_TESTING (default ON) controls them, and
they are left out when cross compiling, since they run disparPDFc.

- batch-legacy runs the existing test/testbase.sh, which still passes.
- 24 new tests run disparPDFc on small PDFs in test/data (see its
  README) and check the result code it prints and how many pages of
  differences it saves (test/runtest.cpp; settings such as margins and
  zoom are passed with --settings).  They cover identical content, a
  changed word, reflowed text, lines drawn in a different order, a page
  before and after rewriting with Ghostscript, a line drawn twice, boxes
  inside and outside a top margin at zoom 100% and 200%, an inserted
  page with --startPage1/--startPage2, and --help.

The PDFs were made by test/data/make-test-pdfs.sh (with fonts embedded,
so testing needs no Ghostscript or fonts), except the rewritten page,
which is from a technical report by Barak A. Pearlmutter, contributed
under GPL-2+.

Against the code before this series (7680a57) exactly five of the new
tests fail, one for each of the fixes since: bold-appearance
(antialiasing), margins-zoom200-box (margin region at other zooms),
inserted-start-pages (--startPage2), and rewritten-characters and
rewritten-words (word order).

[Debian: the test PDFs are left out of this patch, as quilt patches
cannot hold binary files; debian/rules copies them in from
debian/test-data.]

